{
  "name": "core",
  "reviewed_duckdb": "1.5.5",
  "source": "https://github.com/duckdb/duckdb/tree/d8cdaa33fda8df955cc76ef58a280f68f4cd43fa",
  "notes": [
    "Unlisted names remain excluded pending source review.",
    "Classification criteria: compute names have no effect beyond their arguments except the transaction-start clock and the connection-local random engine; elevated names read catalog, session, configuration, or planner state, perform I/O or mutation, dispatch by caller-supplied name, consume resources, or are internal/debug registrations that are not a supported caller surface (see inventories/README.md).",
    "Clock functions now/get_current_timestamp/transaction_timestamp (extension/core_functions/scalar/date/current.cpp) and the macros ago/pg_conf_load_time/pg_postmaster_start_time return MetaTransaction start_timestamp, a per-transaction constant; they disclose only wall-clock time.",
    "random/uuid/uuidv4/uuidv7/gen_random_uuid draw from the connection-local PCG32 RandomEngine (extension/core_functions/scalar/random/random.cpp); setseed writes only that engine's seed, which is consumed solely by those functions and unseeded SAMPLE (src/execution/physical_plan/plan_sample.cpp). Not a CSPRNG; never a secret.",
    "apply/filter/reduce are registered aliases of list_transform/list_filter/list_reduce (extension/core_functions/scalar/list/functions.json) and must share their classification; test_inventory.py enforces alias consistency.",
    "compatibility_stubs are PostgreSQL macros from src/catalog/default/default_functions.cpp that expand to constants ('duckdb', true, false, 0, NULL), an identity, a CASE over the argument, or a compute function (pg_typeof -> lower(typeof), pg_size_pretty -> format_bytes). format_type is not a stub: it selects from duckdb_types() and is elevated.",
    "version()/pragma_version() report the engine version and source id, which Gatekeeper pins and advertises in its own load error and descriptor; pragma_platform and pragma_user_agent reveal host OS/arch/client and are elevated.",
    "duckdb_keywords (Parser::KeywordList) and duckdb_optimizers (ListAllOptimizers) are static embedded lists. summary (src/function/table/summary.cpp) stringifies its own input rows. array_to_string_comma_default is a fixed-name list macro over string_agg, like list_sum.",
    "st_asbinary/st_astext/st_aswkb/st_aswkt/st_crs/st_geomfromwkb/st_intersects_extent/st_setcrs are core GEOMETRY serialization functions (src/function/scalar/geometry/geometry_functions.cpp) with no PROJ, catalog, or filesystem access; the spatial extension's overloads of four of these names are reviewed at its pinned revision (see extensions/spatial.json).",
    "read_duckdb attaches a hidden database during binding (src/function/table/read_duckdb.cpp).",
    "histogram shares a name with a table macro that calls query_table; classify the most capable overload, not only the compute aggregate. histogram_values has the same dynamic-table behavior (src/catalog/default/default_table_functions.cpp).",
    "aggregate/array_aggr/array_aggregate/list_aggr/list_aggregate dispatch an argument-selected catalog aggregate, unlike fixed-name list macros (extension/core_functions/scalar/list/list_aggregates.cpp). current_setting can autoload extensions during binding (scalar/generic/current_setting.cpp).",
    "combine/finalize look up the aggregate named inside an AGGREGATE_STATE type in the system catalog (src/function/scalar/system/aggregate_export.cpp): dispatch. make_type evaluates its arguments at bind time and resolves the named type through Binder::BindLogicalType, which can consult the catalog and autoload extensions (extension/core_functions/scalar/generic/type_functions.cpp).",
    "current_query returns the full statement text, which exposes any host-authored wrapper SQL around tenant text. txid_current/current_transaction_id/current_query_id/current_connection_id expose instance-wide activity counters. stats exposes planner statistics (min/max/null counts) of the underlying column even through a filtering view. parse_duckdb_log_message probes the LogManager type registry. These are elevated as session or planner inspection.",
    "pg_sleep/sleep_ms consume wall time on the executing connection. seq_scan scans a table by internal name and is on the never-bind list. pandas_scan/python_map_function/arrow_scan take raw POINTER arguments. __internal_compress_*/__internal_decompress_*, vector_type, test_all_types, and test_vector_types are optimizer, debug, or test registrations that DuckDB does not harden as a caller surface.",
    "The Python baseline does not cover every optional extension; proprietary/runtime-only limits remain in extension inventories."
  ],
